/E (The Alkebuleum mainnet \(and by extension the Foundation/DAO governance\) could have a role in managing the registry of official subchains. Perhaps new subchains have to be approved by governance if they want to be recognized at the protocol level \(for instance, to use the AKE token or to share security\). Over time, governance could become decentralized among all AKE holders, meaning the community can vote to accept or reject new subchains into the ecosystem based on their merit and security model. This multi-chain approach is forward-looking but realistic: networks like Polkadot use a relay-chain & parachains model, and Cosmos enables sovereign interoperable zones.)
